 "source": "GLM-5.3's sparse-attention rows (the row family SparseMlaSplit_v1 of the served circuit's census, every rank, one request of 256 prompt tokens and 32 steps) partitioned by benchmarks/one_stage/block_census.py at tree d012feea83: each head's key block its scores unit (SparseMlaHeadScores_v1: the block's running max, sums and bf16 probabilities) and its values units on 64 columns (SparseMlaHeadValues_v1, each reading the scores unit's probabilities), a split's end on each column block, the combine of each column block of the splits, and a head's end; a key block stays whole where a unit of it fits no proof block. Units a token are the census's counts over 287 tokens; output bits, input bits and MACs from each Definition; ANDs the estimator's upper bound on the word form; k_log the block Flock's range rule stages each at (benchmarks/one_stage/m1_families.block). None of these types is measured by the proof_overhead card, so Figure 1 prices them by their k_log. The Definitions are on main and circuit-checked; the vLLM adapter's serving of them is in review; nothing is measured or served. Each unit commits its own row of the block's keys and no unit writes that row, so nothing holds two units' keys equal: the strata are a cost model's, not a bound under the guarantees.",
